  <Docs>
    <summary>Information about a one-time agent-related event to communicate to the user.</summary>
    <remarks>
      <para>An event temporarily occupies status-bar space and can hide the current state icon. It must contain text, icons, or both. Content appears in the order leading icons, text, then trailing icons, with empty parts omitted.</para>
      <para>Space limits can shorten or omit content. The system can suppress an event when events arrive too frequently, the status bar is hidden, or more important status information must be shown.</para>
    </remarks>
  </Docs>
